ry  required  and finally accuracy is improved as the  sop version control is now done  inside the counter itself so  administrators log on remotely via web  browser there's no  software required and they configure the  sop and they release it using their  electronic signatures for use by their  technicians  clarity software creates the final  electronic record  inside the counter contemporaneously  there's no more need for paper printouts  or made to manual data transcription  because the record it creates contains  the sop name  and the version number that was used  when the technician did the test  it contains the user electronic  signature which is controlled by  microsoft active directory it contains  the product production batch id the  location name  date and time configuration of the  counter sampling results including the  volume of sample taken  and of course any alert and action  alarms  and the user can manually enter through  the counter screen  using a qwerty keyboard any comments  which are saved with the electronic  record  there is also review and approved  workflow built into clarity which sits  inside the air particle counter  so the clarity software allows the  administrator or the supervisor to log  in  remotely over their corporate network  using  a web browser there's no specialist  software required  the clarity workflow inside the counter  allows the date  sampling to be reviewed and approved for  accuracy  remotely just using this web browser  interface  and then it creates an electronic record  with the electronic signature attached  of the supervisor or the administrator  ready to export straight from the  counter via  usb or wired ethernet or wi-fi  the counter also contains an integrated  audit trail which again helps with  accuracy  any changes to the user id or  anything like that is recorded in there  user logons success and failures log out  sample start sample completion new users  added  changes changes to an sop all of this is  recorded inside the  audit trail in the particle counter  itself  that forms an electronic record which  again can be exported  so that was a quick quick overview of  the clarity software that's inside the  new met 13400 plus  and um i hope you can see how it should  help with uh  improve the data integrity for these  very manual processes  so thank you for listening today i hope  you found it informative and and now  perhaps michelle if we can  go to any questions that you may have in  the chat please  absolutely thank you tony for your  presentation  we'll now start the q a portion of the  webinar if you have a question you'd  like to ask  please do so now just click on the ask a  question box  located on the far left of your screen  we'll answer as many  questions as we have time for all right  let's go ahead and get started  okay first question tony thank you for  your presentation  please can you tell me how you can use a  web browser to remotely review and  approve  daily environmental monitoring data  is the counter connected to the internet  well thank you very much for your  question it's a good question  so no the counter is not connected to  the internet what actually happens is  the counter  has its own web server inside the  clarity software  so what you do is you use your web  browser to connect across your company  internal network to the counter  you simply enter the ip address of your  network assigns to the counter  when it connects to your network into  your own web browser navigation bar  and the ip address can be found on the  front screen of the counter  itself  great thank you so much okay let's see  next question how does the counter  assign  electronic signatures to the records  that's a good question thank you and as  i mentioned i think a couple of times in  the presentation the counter  actually uses microsoft active directory  to control  username and password credentials so  when somebody logs on to the counter  using their  active direc