ecorded inside the  audit trail in the particle counter  itself  that forms an electronic record which  again can be exported  so that was a quick quick overview of  the clarity software that's inside the  new met 13400 plus  and um i hope you can see how it should  help with uh  improve the data integrity for these  very manual processes  so thank you for listening today i hope  you found it informative and and now  perhaps michelle if we can  go to any questions that you may have in  the chat please  absolutely thank you tony for your  presentation  we'll now start the q a portion of the  webinar if you have a question you'd  like to ask  please do so now just click on the ask a  question box  located on the far left of your screen  we'll answer as many  questions as we have time for all right  let's go ahead and get started  okay first question tony thank you for  your presentation  please can you tell me how you can use a  web browser to remotely review and  approve  daily environmental monitoring data  is the counter connected to the internet  well thank you very much for your  question it's a good question  so no the counter is not connected to  the internet what actually happens is  the counter  has its own web server inside the  clarity software  so what you do is you use your web  browser to connect across your company  internal network to the counter  you simply enter the ip address of your  network assigns to the counter  when it connects to your network into  your own web browser navigation bar  and the ip address can be found on the  front screen of the counter  itself  great thank you so much okay let's see  next question how does the counter  assign  electronic signatures to the records  that's a good question thank you and as  i mentioned i think a couple of times in  the presentation the counter  actually uses microsoft active directory  to control  username and password credentials so  when somebody logs on to the counter  using their  active directory credentials the counter  goes across the end corporate network  and verifies that the credentials  they've used  match the active directory on the  network and then assigns the username to  the electronic record  so effectively your microsoft active  directory credentials become the  electronic signature  and it's the same verification process  that happens when you log on to your own  computer when you log on for the day you  go to work you log on using the  microsoft active directory  username and password  thanks tony and let's go ahead and wrap  up with this last question  how do i know if the technician used the  correct sop  version when they did their daily  sampling  yeah again that's so that's the typical  challenge that people face  because these are typically paper based  but now all the sop version control is  done  inside the counter using the clarity  software  the technicians only have access to the  latest version of the sop  on the counter and this is controlled by  the manager or the administrator  who programmed the current sop version  into the counter  and they release it for use using their  electronic signature again using  microsoft active directory  and so you can verify which i think was  the question  which sop version which was used because  the sop  name and version number used is recorded  in every electronic record that the  clarity software  creates  thank you again tony for your time today  and your research  we would also like to thank labrus and  our sponsor  beckman coulter life sciences for  underwriting today's  educational webcast before we go  i'd like to thank the audience for  joining us today and further questions  any questions we did not have time for  today and those submitted  during the on-demand period will be  addressed by tony via the contact  information you provided  at the time of registration this webcast  can be viewed on demand  laborers will alert you via email when  it's available for replay  we encourage you to share that email  with your colleagues who may have missed  today's event  until next time goodbye


